{
  "case_id": "2020-20-543",
  "document_hash": "d293fbb46078af1619a52cbb6f1a5589aee4db266079b33a1a3650709d04d908",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-20-543",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d293fbb46078af1619a52cbb6f1a5589aee4db266079b33a1a3650709d04d908",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d293fbb46078-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:00 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Secretary of the Treasury (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2020-20-543",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d293fbb46078af1619a52cbb6f1a5589aee4db266079b33a1a3650709d04d908",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d293fbb46078-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our fundamental submission in this case is that in defining \"Indian Tribe\" for ISDA purposes, Congress did not deliberately include Alaska native regional and village corporations only to then exclude all of them by subjecting them to a formal political recognition requirement that no ANC meets or, indeed, has ever met."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Secretary of the Treasury (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2020-20-543",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d293fbb46078af1619a52cbb6f1a5589aee4db266079b33a1a3650709d04d908",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d293fbb46078-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress was acting against the backdrop of those settled understandings when it incorporated the ISDA definition of \"Indian Tribe\" into the CARES Act in 2020."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2020-20-543",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d293fbb46078af1619a52cbb6f1a5589aee4db266079b33a1a3650709d04d908",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d293fbb46078-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice. Counsel, would you give us again -- would you repeat -- maybe I missed it -- your -- your textual argument again?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2020-20-543",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d293fbb46078af1619a52cbb6f1a5589aee4db266079b33a1a3650709d04d908",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d293fbb46078-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: I -- I'm just curious as to whether -- what CARES Act expenditures necessary related to COVID, et cetera -- do the Alaska corporations make that kind of expenditure?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2020-20-543",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d293fbb46078af1619a52cbb6f1a5589aee4db266079b33a1a3650709d04d908",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d293fbb46078-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: And, if so, is the federal government prepared to step in and provide those services?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2020-20-543",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d293fbb46078af1619a52cbb6f1a5589aee4db266079b33a1a3650709d04d908",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d293fbb46078-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What -- what's your response to that argument?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Guarnieri",
      "case_id": "2020-20-543",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d293fbb46078af1619a52cbb6f1a5589aee4db266079b33a1a3650709d04d908",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d293fbb46078-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We do -- we do agree with that. We have grave concerns about what the effects of affirming the D.C. Circuit's decision here would be on a wide range of other federal programs."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2020-20-543",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d293fbb46078af1619a52cbb6f1a5589aee4db266079b33a1a3650709d04d908",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d293fbb46078-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "How much money is exactly at stake and what will happen to it if you lose?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Guarnieri",
      "case_id": "2020-20-543",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d293fbb46078af1619a52cbb6f1a5589aee4db266079b33a1a3650709d04d908",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d293fbb46078-0001-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Initially, the Department of Treasury allocated about 6 percent of this 8 billion dollar fund to the ANCs, which is about $530 million."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Guarnieri",
      "case_id": "2020-20-543",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d293fbb46078af1619a52cbb6f1a5589aee4db266079b33a1a3650709d04d908",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d293fbb46078-0001-0012",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First, ISDA's definition of \"Indian Tribes\" should not be read to be at war with itself. Congress did not deliberately and specifically include ANCs in one clause only to then exclude them in the very next clause."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Clement",
      "case_id": "2020-20-543",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d293fbb46078af1619a52cbb6f1a5589aee4db266079b33a1a3650709d04d908",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d293fbb46078-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress established ANCs in the Settlement Act as native entities unlike lower 48 tribes. ANCs have never been sovereign, but they have always played a critical role in distributing special federal Indian benefits to Alaska natives."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2020-20-543",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d293fbb46078af1619a52cbb6f1a5589aee4db266079b33a1a3650709d04d908",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d293fbb46078-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Did the -- what's the overlap between the ANCs and the 200-plus tribes in -- in Alaska?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Clement",
      "case_id": "2020-20-543",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d293fbb46078af1619a52cbb6f1a5589aee4db266079b33a1a3650709d04d908",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d293fbb46078-0001-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There are many, many, you know, tens of thousands, Alaska natives who are shareholders of an ANC but not enrolled members of any village-type tribe."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Clement",
      "case_id": "2020-20-543",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d293fbb46078af1619a52cbb6f1a5589aee4db266079b33a1a3650709d04d908",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d293fbb46078-0001-0009",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Alaska natives will go radically underserved if the ANCs are cut out of the statute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2020-20-543",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d293fbb46078af1619a52cbb6f1a5589aee4db266079b33a1a3650709d04d908",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d293fbb46078-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is there a difference between your interpretation of the recognition clause and the Solicitor General's interpretation? And if there is a difference, what do you understand it to be?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2020-20-543",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d293fbb46078af1619a52cbb6f1a5589aee4db266079b33a1a3650709d04d908",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d293fbb46078-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "none had been recognized in the sense that the D.C. Circuit thought was necessary. Are those two points correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2020-20-543",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d293fbb46078af1619a52cbb6f1a5589aee4db266079b33a1a3650709d04d908",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d293fbb46078-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I mean, I understand that, but doesn't Congress's use of that phrase in the List Act undercut your argument that eligibility isn't about sovereignty?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Rasmussen",
      "case_id": "2020-20-543",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "d293fbb46078af1619a52cbb6f1a5589aee4db266079b33a1a3650709d04d908",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d293fbb46078-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And so, in our -- in our brief to this Court, we discuss that in the very next section of the CARES Act Congress does exactly that. It refers to cities, towns, parishes that -- that are over 500,000 people. And Congress, in that case, could have simply looked at a census and said: Oh, parish -- there's no parish over 500,000. We should take that out. But, under the ANCs' argument, because it included parishes and then it included a qualifier that plainly didn't apply to parishes, all the parishes should have gotten money."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2020-20-543",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "d293fbb46078af1619a52cbb6f1a5589aee4db266079b33a1a3650709d04d908",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d293fbb46078-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, why would Congress put ANCs in the language and then take them out? I mean, is it -- is your argument based solely on the uncertainty that at some point in the future the Congress might undo the whole ANCSA approach based on Congress's -- Alaska's distinct situation?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2020-20-543",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "d293fbb46078af1619a52cbb6f1a5589aee4db266079b33a1a3650709d04d908",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d293fbb46078-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Counsel, why do you think the Congress cross-referenced ISDA rather than simply the list of recognized tribes?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Rasmussen",
      "case_id": "2020-20-543",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "d293fbb46078af1619a52cbb6f1a5589aee4db266079b33a1a3650709d04d908",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d293fbb46078-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "doesn't agree with it -- but we --we believe that there was substantial uncertainty in 1975. That's certainly what the court of appeals found, that there was sufficient uncertainty."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2020-20-543",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "d293fbb46078af1619a52cbb6f1a5589aee4db266079b33a1a3650709d04d908",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d293fbb46078-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And what do you make of the -- of the ratification argument?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2020-20-543",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "d293fbb46078af1619a52cbb6f1a5589aee4db266079b33a1a3650709d04d908",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d293fbb46078-0003-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 71,
        "start": 71
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is my question absurd? Do you have a problem?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Rasmussen",
      "case_id": "2020-20-543",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "d293fbb46078af1619a52cbb6f1a5589aee4db266079b33a1a3650709d04d908",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d293fbb46078-0003-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 76,
        "start": 76
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We don't go and do that research to find out what exactly -- whether there would be any possibility of an ANC qualifying. The Congress wouldn't do that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Rasmussen",
      "case_id": "2020-20-543",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "d293fbb46078af1619a52cbb6f1a5589aee4db266079b33a1a3650709d04d908",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d293fbb46078-0003-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 81,
        "start": 81
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What we have actually is the ANCs themselves saying Congress could do this under its plenary power. Plenary power is very, very broad."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GORSUCH",
      "case_id": "2020-20-543",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d293fbb46078af1619a52cbb6f1a5589aee4db266079b33a1a3650709d04d908",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d293fbb46078-0004-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 84,
        "start": 84
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "About 530 million dollars."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. RASMUSSEN",
      "case_id": "2020-20-543",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d293fbb46078af1619a52cbb6f1a5589aee4db266079b33a1a3650709d04d908",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d293fbb46078-0004-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 84,
        "start": 84
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, about 71 million dollars, if I recall correctly, was allocated to the population of ANCs."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GORSUCH",
      "case_id": "2020-20-543",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d293fbb46078af1619a52cbb6f1a5589aee4db266079b33a1a3650709d04d908",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d293fbb46078-0004-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 85,
        "start": 85
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "All right. Then let me -- let me try my question again, though. Mr. Clement says there are administrative ways to deal with that problem and that, therefore, we're really fighting over nothing here. Why isn't that correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. RASMUSSEN",
      "case_id": "2020-20-543",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d293fbb46078af1619a52cbb6f1a5589aee4db266079b33a1a3650709d04d908",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d293fbb46078-0004-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 94,
        "start": 94
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, I -- I think, you know, I would not question that they know Alaska, but I think they also are motivated by getting $533 million up into Alaska instead of into the lower 40 -- mostly into the lower 48 states, divided amongst all the tribes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2020-20-543",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d293fbb46078af1619a52cbb6f1a5589aee4db266079b33a1a3650709d04d908",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d293fbb46078-0005-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 105,
        "start": 105
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And as I think Justice Alito's perceptive questions have pointed out, I mean, it makes no sense to think that the CARES Act incorporated for a -- purposes of a one-time distribution of funds, the CARES Act incorporated a definition under which ANCs would be included only if at some theoretical point in the future Congress chooses to fundamentally reinvent the concept of recognition and recognize as eligible for government-to-government relations these private corporations."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2020-20-543",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d293fbb46078af1619a52cbb6f1a5589aee4db266079b33a1a3650709d04d908",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d293fbb46078-0005-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 107,
        "start": 107
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: -- thank you, counsel. The case is submitted. (Whereupon, at 11:44 a.m., the case was submitted.)"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2020-20-543",
